Unfortunately this would fail to catch nested sensitive values. For example, it would cause this to happen:

```hcl
output "a" {
  value = {
    b = sensitive("foo")
  }
}
```

```
Changes to Outputs:
  + a = {
      + b = "foo"
    }
```

Whereas with the code as-is, we get:

```
│ Error: Output refers to sensitive values
│
│   on main.tf line 1:
│    1: output "a" {
│
│ Expressions used in outputs can only refer to sensitive values if the sensitive attribute is true.
```
